-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",418,{
[13345]="70022443\n1\tTalk to the Wild Huntsman in the Huntsman's Hall\tThe Wild Huntsman resides in the Huntsman's Hall. You have been instructed to approach the Huntsman and ask that the Grey Company be allowed to pass through the southern Mournshaws into Dunland.\n2\tHunt Munfaeril's spirit\030Hunt Gwenaewen's spirit\030Hunt Lavaneth's spirit\tThe servants of the Wild Huntsman are in the Huntsman's Hall. The Huntsman has bidden you complete the tasks that the his hand-maidens set before you.\n3\tHunt Arassiel's spirit\tArassiel is at the Huntsman's Hall. One last spirit remains to be challenged. You should speak with Arassiel and hunt as she bids you.\n4\tTalk to the Wild Huntsman in the Huntsman's Hall\tThe Wild Huntsman is at the Huntsman's Hall. Having completed the Wild Hunt, you should return and speak with the Huntsman on behalf of the Dúnedain.\n",
[13346]="70022383\n1\tChallenge Arassiel's spirit\tThe stag-spirit of Arassiel dwells in the southern reaches of the Mournshaws. Arassiel has charged you with challenging her stag-spirit servant.\n2\tTalk to Arassiel at the Huntsman's Hall\tArassiel is in the Huntsman's Hall. You should return to Arassiel with news of your success.\n",
[13347]="70021FB5\n1\tChallenge Gwenaewen's spirit\tGwenaewen's spirit dwells in the heart of the Mournshaws. Gwenaewen has charged you with hunting her falcon-spirit servant.\n2\tTalk to Gwenaewen at the Huntsman's Hall\tGwenaewen is at the Huntsman's Hall. You should return to Gwenaewen and tell her that you have overcome her challenge.\n",
[13348]="70022384\n1\tChallenge Lavaneth's spirit\tLavaneth's spirit roams in the north-west eaves of the Mournshaws. Lavaneth has bidden you hunt her boar-spirit.\n2\tTalk to Lavaneth at the Huntsman's Hall\tLavaneth is at the Huntsman's Hall. You should return to Lavaneth and tell her of your successful challenge against the boar-spirit.\n",
[13349]="70021FB4\n1\tChallenge Munfaeril's Spirit\tThe ox-spirit dwells beneath the north-east eaves of the Mournshaws. Munfaeril has bidden you challenge her ox-spirit servant.\n2\tTalk to Munfaeril at the Huntsman's Hall\tMunfaeril is at the Huntsman's Hall. You should return to Munfaeril and tell her of your success in the challenge of endurance.\n",
[13350]="70059838\n1\tThe great beasts can be found across the Wildwood. Linnet has asked you to defeat the White Stag Gwengorn, the Great Boar Brundurch, the Black Elk Dúgar, and the Silver Warg Lhudblath.\t\n2\tReturn to Linnet\tLinnet can be found in the central Wildwood. You should return to Linnet.\n",
[13351]="70059323\n1\tTalk to Aran Greenwith\030Talk to Enid Nettlesting\tAran Greenwith can be found at Trestlebridge and Enid Nettlesting can be found at Trader's Wharf. You should talk to Aran Greenwith and Enid Nettlesting.\n",
[13352]="700551E0\n1\tSearch slain Orcs and uruks for orders from Ugrukhôr\tSlain Orcs and Uruk-hai can be found in the Circle of Despair. You should search fallen Orcs and Uruk-hai for orders from Ugrukhôr. NOTE: If you lose sight of Dornach, you can summon him to your side with his horn.\n2\tSearch slain Orcs and Uruk-hai for orders from Ugrukhôr\tSlain Orcs and Uruk-hai can be found in the Circle of Despair. You should search fallen Orcs and Uruk-hai for orders from Ugrukhôr. NOTE: If you lose sight of Dornach, you can summon him to your side with his horn.\n3\tDeliver the orders from Ugrukhôr to Dornach\tDornach can be found in the Circle of Despair. You have found orders from Ugrukhôr carried by a slain Uruk-hai. You should deliver them to Dornach. NOTE: If you lose sight of Dornach, you can summon him to your side with his horn.\n",
[13353]="700174AA\n1\tFind the Western Gate of the Twenty-first Hall\tWárr is in the Chamber of Mazarbul, just north of the Twenty-first Hall, far to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads. You must travel east from the Chamber of the Cross-roads through the great winding road leading to the Twenty-first Hall.\n2\tTalk to Wárr\tWárr is in the Chamber of Mazarbul, north of the Twenty-first Hall, far to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads. Líkmund has asked you to speak with Wárr and relay what you know of recent events from the Chamber of the Cross-roads.\n",
[13354]="70046BFC\n1\tSit near Dornach and allow him to blindfold you\tDornach can be found along the road to the north of Aelin Veren in North Ithilien. Dornach has asked you to sit near him, so he can blindfold you for your journey to Henneth Annûn.\n2\tTravel with Dornach to Henneth Annûn\tDornach is leading you to the hidden refuge of Henneth Annûn.\n3\tTalk to Dornach at Henneth Annûn\tDornach can be found within Henneth Annûn. Dornach has led you to the hidden refuge of Henneth Annûn. You should now speak to him.\n",
[13355]="7004135E\n1\tEnter the wine cellar\tThe wine cellar is located in the village of Gaerlond. You should enter the wine cellar.\n2\tDefeat drunk Corsairs (total: 3)\tThe drunk corsairs can be found in the wine cellar in Gaerlond. You should defeat the drunk corsairs.\n3\tRetrieve any unopened wine bottles for Túmir\tWine can be found in the wine cellar in Gaerlond. You should retrieve any unopened wine bottles for Túmir.\n4\tReturn to Túmir with the bottle of wine\tTúmir can be found in the village of Gaerlond. You should return to Túmir with the bottle of wine.\n",
[13356]="700001A4\n1\tDefeat merrevail in Himbar (total: 3)\030Defeat bats in Himbar (total: 5)\tThe merrevail and the bats hunt throughout Himbar, the lands west of Gath Forthnír. Thoriel warned you of the merrevail, winged monsters in service to the Enemy. They prey upon the Rangers and must be destroyed, along with their lesser kindred, the bats.\n2\tTalk to Thoriel\tThoriel waits for you in Gath Forthnír, the hidden Ranger camp east of Himbar. You defeated the winged servants of the Enemy and may now return to claim victory.\n",
[13357]="7004956B\n1\tZôreth's chambers can be found upon the highest level of the Oath-taker's Horn. Gimli has asked you to seek out Zôreth's research in her chambers of old in the hope that it might lead you to King Greytooth and the Firehorns.\t\n2\tDeliver to Zôreth's research to Spakorth in the Oath-taker's Horn\tSpakorth can be found in Zôreth's chambers within the Oath-taker's Horn. You have found much of Zôreth's research into the locations of Sauron's artifacts. You should deliver the pages you recovered to Spakorth.\n",
[13358]="70067164\n1\tFind Dejeni's father Mulúgu by the throne of Furukzahar\tDejeni's father Mulúgu fought in the Battle of Azanulbizar and will tell you about it if you find him by the throne of Furukzahar.\n2\tTalk to Dejeni in the feast-hall of Furukzahar\tMulúgu was sleeping, and you chose not to bother him. Perhaps Dejeni will tell you about the Battle of Azanulbizar instead.\n",
[13359]="70007826\n1\tDraw water from the Staddle town well\tThe Staddle town well is in Staddle town centre. To find the Silverwater Spring, take the road east from the town square to the Widow Froghorn's farm, then south to Constable Bolger's house. The Silverwater Spring is south-east of there. Draw a bucket of water from the well and bring it to Willowsong.\n2\tBring the bucket of poisoned water to Willowsong\tWillowsong is at Silverwater Spring. You drew a bucket of water from the Staddle town well and brought it to Willowsong.\n",
[13360]="70031734\n1\tComplete The Witan: Lords of the Eastemnet\tThe Witan is being held at the Mead Hall of Hytbold. The Lords of Rohan have decided to hold a Witan in Hytbold to determine the fate of the Eastemnet.\n2\tComplete The Witan: The Battle for Hytbold\tEdgal is at the Mead Hall of Hytbold. Hytbold has come under assault from an unknown enemy.\n3\tTalk to Edgal\tEdgal is at the Mead Hall of Hytbold. Edgal will want to speak to you about what has just happened.\n",
[13361]="7003172F\n1\tTalk to Harding to signal the beginning of the Witan\tThe Witan is being held in Hytbold.\n2\tAttend and observe the Witan\tThe Witan has begun and the Lords are discussing the future of the Eastemnet.\n",
[13362]="70031733\n1\tTalk to Harding\tDefend Hytbold at all costs.\n2\tJoin Harding on the north flank\tDefend Hytbold at all costs.\n3\tDefend the north flank\tDefend Hytbold at all costs.\n4\tJoin Ingbert on the south flank\tDefend Hytbold at all costs.\n5\tDefend the south flank\tDefend Hytbold at all costs.\n6\tJoin Ides in the centre\tDefend Hytbold at all costs.\n7\tDefend the centre\tDefend Hytbold at all costs.\n8\tDefeat the troll\tDefend Hytbold at all costs.\n9\tRegroup with the Lords of the Eastemnet\tDefend Hytbold at all costs.\n10\tTalk to Harding\tHarding waits to speak with you.\n",
[13363]="700544D9\n1\tDefeat the Witch-king in Mordor Besieged\tGreatest and most feared of the Nine, the Witch-king stalked the battlefield but rarely, leaving the fortresses of Mordor only at Sauron's most pressing command. In later years the Lord of the Nazgûl would raise from nothing the Land of Angmar, wielding it in furtherance of the Dark Lord's aim to destroy the northern kingdom of Arnor, but at the close of the Second Age that was still far off in the mists of Time. During the Siege of Barad-dûr, the Witch-king could be found testing the weaknesses of the armies arrayed against his master, seeking the most valuable prize of all: information.\n2\tDefeat the Witch-king in Mordor Besieged\tGreatest and most feared of the Nine, the Witch-king stalked the battlefield but rarely, leaving the fortresses of Mordor only at Sauron's most pressing command. In later years the Lord of the Nazgûl would raise from nothing the Land of Angmar, wielding it in furtherance of the Dark Lord's aim to destroy the northern kingdom of Arnor, but at the close of the Second Age that was still far off in the mists of Time. During the Siege of Barad-dûr, the Witch-king could be found testing the weaknesses of the armies arrayed against his master, seeking the most valuable prize of all: information.\n3\tThe Witch-king, Lord of the Nazgûl, defeated but enduring\tGreatest and most feared of the Nine, the Witch-king stalked the battlefield but rarely, leaving the fortresses of Mordor only at Sauron's most pressing command. In later years the Lord of the Nazgûl would raise from nothing the Land of Angmar, wielding it in furtherance of the Dark Lord's aim to destroy the northern kingdom of Arnor, but at the close of the Second Age that was still far off in the mists of Time. During the Siege of Barad-dûr, the Witch-king could be found testing the weaknesses of the armies arrayed against his master, seeking the most valuable prize of all: information.\n",
[13364]="700442AF\n1\tTalk to Húrin in the besieged city, in the Dome of the Sun\tHúrin is in the besieged city, in the Dome of the Sun. Lamlor believes you should ask Húrin to change the pass-words for the gates in the upper Circles of the city. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n2\tDeliver the new pass-word to Linharn at the Gate of the Citadel\030Deliver the new pass-word to Garthor at the Gate of Stones\030Deliver the new pass-word to Doronir at the Gate of Stars\tYou carry new pass-words for the Gate of the Citadel, the Gate of Stones, and the Gate of Stars. Húrin has sent you to deliver the new pass-words for the gates in the upper Circles of the city. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n3\tDestroy the parchment containing the new pass-words\tYou carry new pass-words for the Gate of the Citadel, the Gate of Stones, and the Gate of Stars. Húrin has sent you to deliver new pass-words for the gates in the upper Circles of the city. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n4\tInvestigate the Fourth Circle of the city for supporters of the Withered Tree\tSome of the citizens of Gondor in the Fourth Circle may actually be supporters of the Withered Tree.\n5\tInvestigate the Third Circle of the city for supporters of the Withered Tree\tSome of the citizens of Gondor in the Third Circle may actually be supporters of the Withered Tree.\n6\tInvestigate the Second Circle of the city for supporters of the Withered Tree\tSome of the citizens of Gondor in the Second Circle may actually be supporters of the Withered Tree.\n7\tTalk to Lamlor at the City Gates, in the First Circle\tLamlor, the Captain of Tidings and Spy-master of Gondor, has come down to the gate in the First Circle.\n",
[13365]="700544D4\n1\tDefeat the Woe of Khand in Mordor Besieged\tHe was the Woe of Khand, and with the blessing of Sauron he strode across the unconquered lands and claimed them for the Dark Lord. The ring gifted to him was called Adâsh, and many were the foes it made, many the proud warriors he brought low. He found great joy in the bringing of war, and always had done so, but with the power given to him by Sauron, the Woe of Khand became ever more deadly, more relentless, and more unforgiving.\n2\tDefeat the Woe of Khand in Mordor Besieged\tHe was the Woe of Khand, and with the blessing of Sauron he strode across the unconquered lands and claimed them for the Dark Lord. The ring gifted to him was called Adâsh, and many were the foes it made, many the proud warriors he brought low. He found great joy in the bringing of war, and always had done so, but with the power given to him by Sauron, the Woe of Khand became ever more deadly, more relentless, and more unforgiving.\n3\tThe Woe of Khand, defeated but enduring\tHe was the Woe of Khand, and with the blessing of Sauron he strode across the unconquered lands and claimed them for the Dark Lord. The ring gifted to him was called Adâsh, and many were the foes it made, many the proud warriors he brought low. He found great joy in the bringing of war, and always had done so, but with the power given to him by Sauron, the Woe of Khand became ever more deadly, more relentless, and more unforgiving.\n",
[13366]="7002EA10\n1\tReceive the formal welcome of the Thane\tThane Utred, leader of the northernmost town of the Wold, is in the Mead Hall of Langhold. You should speak with Thane Utred at once to receive a proper welcome to the town.\n",
[13367]="700032BE\n1\tFind Jolly Smallburrow\tJolly Smallburrow may be after the wolf that was seen across the road from the wolf-den, north of Dora Brownlock's farm. Dora Brownlock is worried that her neighbour, Jolly Smallburrow, may be in trouble and has asked you to find him.\n2\tTalk to Dora Brownlock\tDora Brownlock is at the centre of Waymeet. Dora will be pleased to know that you have rescued Jolly Smallburrow and defeated the scarred leader of the wolves that have been harassing her farm and town.\n",
[13368]="70007D70\n1\tTrack the wolves to their den\tThe wolves seem to have come from somewhere south of Thorenhad. You should track the wolves back to their den.\n2\tTrack the wolves south to the main road\tThe wolves seem to have come from somewhere south of Thorenhad. You should track the wolves back to their den.\n3\tTrack the wolves eastward along the road\tThe wolves seem to have come from somewhere south of Thorenhad. Their trail seems to lead eastward along the road. You should track the wolves back to their den.\n4\tTrack the wolves south off the road\tThe wolves seem to have come from somewhere south of Thorenhad. Their trail has turned southward off the road. You should track the wolves back to their den.\n5\tSearch deeper in the wolf-den for the source of the evil\tThe den continues westward into the cliffs. You should search deeper in the dens for the source of the evil presence.\n6\tSearch deeper in the wolf-den for the source of the evil\tThe den continues westward into the cliffs. You should search deeper in the dens for the source of the evil presence.\n7\tDefeat the Shadow-wolf elder\tThe Shadow-wolf elder is at Drauglad, east of Narlinn's camp and south of the road. You should attempt to defeat the Shadow-wolf elder.\n8\tTalk to Fimgris\tFimgris is at Narlinn's camp, west down the main road from the entrance to Drauglad. You should return to Fimgris with news of your discovery within Drauglad.\n",
[13369]="70061D31\n1\tCollect kingsfoil (total: 7)\tKingsfoil can be found at the Howlingstones south-east of Mossward. Collect kingsfoil.\n2\tTalk to Iach\tIach can be found near the eastern gate of Mossward. Return to Iach.\n",
[13370]="70015E40\n1\tDefeat Nûkhud, Wolf-master\tNûkhud, Wolf-master is at Barad Morlas, south-west of Echad Eregion. Dornhador has asked you to find and defeat Nûkhud, Wolf-master, the leader of the wolf-keepers at Barad Morlas.\n2\tTalk to Dornhador at Echad Eregion\tDornhador is at Echad Eregion, north-east of Barad Morlas. You should return to Dornhador with tidings of Nûkhud's downfall.\n",
[13371]="7004CF87\n1\tGather saplings (total: 6)\tSaplings can be found just south of Felegoth. You should gather saplings that are to be planted around the forest.\n2\tClear dead trees (total: 10)\030Plant saplings in fertile soil (quantity: see journal)\tFertile soil and dead trees can both be found throughout Eryn Lasgalen. You should clear away the dead trees and plant the saplings in fertile soil around the forest.\n3\tReturn to Radagast\tYou should return to Radagast, who can be found at the tree nursery just outside of Felegoth.\n",
[13372]="700075B5\n1\tCollect seasoned lumber\030Collect savoury mushrooms (total: 8)\030Collect a bucket of maple sap\tThe mushrooms can be found in the western part of Old Forest, between the Bonfire Glade and Bald Hill. The wood can be collected from the wood-cutter's seasoning pile east of the Bonfire Glade and a little south. The sap can be collected from the old maple growing on Bald Hill, east of the Bonfire Glade. Because Toly Brockhouse, the wood-cutter, has sprained his ankle, he has asked you to gather mushrooms, wood, and maple sap for him.\n2\tBring the mushrooms, sap, and wood to Toly Brockhouse\tDeliver the sap, wood, and mushrooms to Toly Brockhouse near the stables outside of Brandy Hall. The Old Forest surrendered its bounty to you, now you must return to Toly Brockhouse.\n",
[13373]="700577F1\n1\tGo to Shulgmokh\tThe wood-trolls dwelling at Shulgmokh possess the great strength of the natural world, but that power is sharpened by the cruelty and anger of which they have always been possessed. They must be eliminated before they turn this strength upon the folk that live in the Floodfells.\n2\tDefeat wood-trolls in Shulgmokh (total: 8)\tThe wood-trolls dwelling at Shulgmokh possess the great strength of the natural world, but that power is sharpened by the cruelty and anger of which they have always been possessed. They must be eliminated before they turn this strength upon the folk that live in the Floodfells.\n3\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[13374]="7005949C\n1\tComplete quests in the Wildwood (total: 10)\tComplete factionless quests in the Wildwood to assist the Woodcutter's Brotherhood.\n2\tCompleted\tAssisted the Woodcutter's Brotherhood.\n",
[13375]="700529E4\n1\tTalk to the frightened villager\030Talk to the suspicious villager\030Talk to the superstitious villager\tBaradal has asked you to gather information from the villagers in Arhaim. You should attempt to talk to the villagers.\n2\tTalk to Garsind\tOne of the villagers suggested that you speak to Arhaim's chieftain for information. You should talk to Garsind.\n3\tTalk to Baradal\tBaradal can be found in Arhaim, the woodmen village in Duskenvale. You should tell Baradal that the woodmen need to be convinced of your trustworthiness.\n4\tComplete quests in Duskenvale (total: 7)\tThe chieftain of Arhaim, Garsind, has asked you to help the village. You should complete quests in Duskenvale to earn the villagers' trust. Lúfred, Ingelfled, Goslim and Tassila may have quests for you.\n5\tTalk to Garsind\tGarsind can be found in Arhaim, the woodmen village in Duskenvale. You should talk to Garsind.\n6\tTalk to Baradal\tGarsind has told you of Shathur-munzu, the dwarf ruin to the west, and of the monster known as the Shadow Hunter. You should relay this information to Baradal.\n",
[13376]="7005338D\n1\tDefeat Shapag-hai at Lúlstrok (total: 12)\tShapag-hai can be found at Lúlstrok in the north-western reaches of the Gladden Fields. You have encountered more of the Shapag-hai in the Gladden Fields. You should defeat them and drive them back into Moria.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many of the Shapag-hai at Lúlstrok.\n",
})
